  "notes": [
    "Regular -ER verb — follows standard endings in every tense, no exceptions.",
    "Mostly used in the 3rd person (like English \"it happens\"), since its subject is usually an event, not a person: *¿Qué sucede?* (\"What's happening?\").",
    "Also means \"to succeed/follow\" in a lineage/sequence sense (*suceder al trono*, \"to succeed to the throne\"), though the \"to happen\" sense is far more common day-to-day.",
    "*Como sucede en las desérticas rutas patagónicas...* (\"As happens on the desert roads of Patagonia...\")",
    "*Nadie sabe qué sucedió esa noche.* (\"Nobody knows what happened that night.\")",
    "Related: *el suceso* (event/happening, noun), *pasar* (near-synonym, \"to happen\"), *ocurrir* (synonym, \"to occur\")."
  ],
